["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"entity-runtime","stream_identity":"01a0cab7-1ed7-77a5-8384-ff10c92e7ad6","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIGa22bdaf21f4d688bb843ef7ff805deb6319e6b029e4c3d4382dba93ca6fe7f65","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/multi-format-entity-graphs","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":6,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# Story: Render entity graphs for terminals, Mermaid and Graphviz\n\n## Acceptance\n\nThe graph model records whether it represents a lifecycle or references. The entity graph command renders deterministic text, Mermaid, DOT, SVG and HTML. Lifecycle Mermaid uses stateDiagram-v2; references use a flowchart. Names cannot inject syntax in any format, and the refund website quickstart renders the exact shipped Mermaid output.\n\n## Implementation evidence\n\nMoved to implemented on 2026-09-09 after an audit of every non-implemented artifact against `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/roadmap.md` and the crates.\n\n`GraphKind` in `crates/entity-graph/src/graph.rs` records lifecycle versus references; `render.rs` emits text, Mermaid, DOT, SVG and HTML with escaped labels — `CHANGELOG.md` `## [0.16.0]`.\n","relations":[{"derived_from":"epic:generated-entity-surfaces"},{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Lifecycle and reference graphs render deterministically as text, Mermaid, DOT, SVG and HTML.","title":"Render entity graphs for terminals, Mermaid and Graphviz"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIGa22bdaf21f4d688bb843ef7ff805deb6319e6b029e4c3d4382dba93ca6fe7f65","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":6,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIGa22bdaf21f4d688bb843ef7ff805deb6319e6b029e4c3d4382dba93ca6fe7f65"]}]